`s 486.4(1)(a) the offence is one referred to in paragraph (a)` MEANS
        ((NOT offence's `the offence is an offence under this Act as it read from time to time before the day on which subparagraph (a)(ii) comes into force`)
         AND `s 487.04 the provision is on the list` (offence's `the provision of the Code the offence is charged under`) `s 486.4(1)(a)(i) the listed offences`)
     OR (offence's `the offence is an offence under this Act as it read from time to time before the day on which subparagraph (a)(ii) comes into force`
         AND offence's `the conduct alleged would be an offence referred to in subparagraph (a)(i) if it occurred on or after that day`)

