        (`count` offences) AT LEAST 2
    AND any (GIVEN o YIELD `s 486.4(1)(a) the offence is one referred to in paragraph (a)` o) offences

-- 486.4(1) Subject to subsection (2), the presiding judge or justice may make an order directing that any information that could identify the victim or a witness shall not be published ... in proceedings in respect of (a) or (b).
-- src:8881 | 486.4 (1) Subject to subsection (2), the presiding judge or justice may make an order directing that any information that could identify the victim or a witness shall not be published in any document or broadcast or transmitted in any way, in proceedings in respect of
@ref s 486.4(1) (src:8881)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in respect of an offence referred to in paragraph (a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.4(1) the presiding judge or justice may make an order directing that information that could identify the victim or a witness not be published` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are in respect of an offence referred to in paragraph (a) or (b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in proceedings in respect of"

-- 486.4(2) In proceedings in respect of the offences referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b), the presiding judge or justice shall (a) as soon as feasible, inform any witness under the age of 18 years and the victim of the
-- right to make an application for the order; (b) on application made by the victim, the prosecutor or any such witness, make the order; and (c) if an order is made, as soon as feasible, inform the witnesses and the victim
-- who are the subject of that order of its existence and of their right to apply to revoke or vary it.
-- src:8887 | (2) In proceedings in respect of the offences referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b), the presiding judge or justice shall
-- src:8888 | (a) as soon as feasible, inform any witness under the age of 18 years and the victim of the right to make an application for the order;
@ref s 486.4(2)(a) (src:8887-8888)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in respect of the offences referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the victim or a witness under the age of 18 years` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.4(2)(a) the presiding judge or justice must inform the person of the right to make an application for the order` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the proceedings are in respect of the offences referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b)` AND `the person is the victim or a witness under the age of 18 years`))
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In proceedings in respect of the offences referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b), the presiding judge or justice shall (a) as soon as feasible, inform any witness under the age of 18 years and the victim"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:8887 | (2) In proceedings in respect of the offences referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b), the presiding judge or justice shall
-- src:8889 | (b) on application made by the victim, the prosecutor or any such witness, make the order; and
@ref s 486.4(2)(b) (src:8887-8889)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in respect of the offences referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `who applies for the order` IS A `s 486.4 who applies`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.4(2)(b) the presiding judge or justice must make the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the proceedings are in respect of the offences referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b)`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In proceedings in respect of the offences referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b)"
        IF ((`who applies for the order` EQUALS `s 486.4 the victim`) OR (`who applies for the order` EQUALS `s 486.4 the prosecutor`) OR (`who applies for the order` EQUALS `s 486.4 a witness under the age of 18 years`)) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application made by the victim, the prosecutor or any such witness, make the order"

-- src:8887 | (2) In proceedings in respect of the offences referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b), the presiding judge or justice shall
-- src:8890 | (c) if an order is made, as soon as feasible, inform the witnesses and the victim who are the subject of that order of its existence and of their right to apply to revoke or vary it.
@ref s 486.4(2)(c) (src:8887-8890)
GIVEN `an order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.4(2)(c) the presiding judge or justice must inform the witnesses and the victim of the order's existence and of their right to apply to revoke or vary it` MEANS
    IF `an order is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if an order is made, as soon as feasible, inform the witnesses and the victim who are the subject of that order"

-- 486.4(2.1) Subject to subsection (2.2), in proceedings in respect of an offence other than an offence referred to in subsection (1), if the victim is under the age of 18 years, the presiding judge or justice may make an order directing
-- that any information that could identify the victim shall not be published in any document or broadcast or transmitted in any way.
