-- 486.4(3) In proceedings in respect of an offence under section 163.1, a judge or justice shall make an order directing that any information that could identify a witness who is under the age of eighteen years, or any
-- person who is the subject of a representation, written material or a recording that constitutes child sexual abuse and exploitation material within the meaning of that section, shall not be published.
-- src:8899 | (3) In proceedings in respect of an offence under section 163.1, a judge or justice shall make an order directing that any information that could identify a witness who is under the age of eighteen years, or any person who is the subject of a representation, written material or a recording that constitutes child sexual abuse and exploitation material within the meaning of that section, shall not be published in any document or broadcast or transmitted in any way.
@ref s 486.4(3) (src:8899)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under section 163.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a witness who is under the age of eighteen years` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 163.1 child sexual abuse and exploitation material: the person is the subject of a representation, written material or a recording that constitutes child sexual abuse and exploitation material` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.4(3) the judge or justice must make an order directing that information that could identify the person not be published` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under section 163.1`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In proceedings in respect of an offence under section 163.1"
        IF `the person is a witness who is under the age of eighteen years` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`s 163.1 child sexual abuse and exploitation material: the person is the subject of a representation, written material or a recording that constitutes child sexual abuse and exploitation material` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a witness who is under the age of eighteen years, or any person who is the subject of a representation, written material or a recording that constitutes child sexual abuse and exploitation material within the meaning of that section"

-- 486.4(3.1) If the prosecutor makes an application for an order under paragraph (2)(b) or (2.2)(b), the presiding judge or justice shall (a) if the victim or witness is present, inquire of the victim or witness if they wish to be the
-- subject of the order; (b) if the victim or witness is not present, inquire of the prosecutor if, before the application was made, they determined if the victim or witness wishes to be the subject of the order; and (c) in any
-- event, advise the prosecutor of their duty under subsection (3.2).
DECLARE `s 486.4(3.1) whom the presiding judge or justice must inquire of` IS ONE OF
    `s 486.4(3.1) the victim or witness, whether they wish to be the subject of the order`
    `s 486.4(3.1) the prosecutor, whether before the application was made they determined if the victim or witness wishes to be the subject of the order`

-- src:8900 | Inquiry by court
-- src:8901 | (3.1) If the prosecutor makes an application for an order under paragraph (2)(b) or (2.2)(b), the presiding judge or justice shall
-- src:8902 | (a) if the victim or witness is present, inquire of the victim or witness if they wish to be the subject of the order;
-- src:8903 | (b) if the victim or witness is not present, inquire of the prosecutor if, before the application was made, they determined if the victim or witness wishes to be the subject of the order; and
@ref s 486.4(3.1)(a), (b) (src:8900-8903)
GIVEN `the prosecutor makes an application for an order under paragraph (2)(b) or (2.2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the victim or witness is present` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 486.4(3.1) whom the presiding judge or justice must inquire of`
`s 486.4(3.1)(a), (b) the presiding judge or justice must inquire` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the prosecutor makes an application for an order under paragraph (2)(b) or (2.2)(b)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the prosecutor makes an application for an order under paragraph (2)(b) or (2.2)(b)"
    ELSE IF `the victim or witness is present`
         THEN JUST `s 486.4(3.1) the victim or witness, whether they wish to be the subject of the order`
         ELSE JUST `s 486.4(3.1) the prosecutor, whether before the application was made they determined if the victim or witness wishes to be the subject of the order`

-- src:8900 | Inquiry by court
-- src:8901 | (3.1) If the prosecutor makes an application for an order under paragraph (2)(b) or (2.2)(b), the presiding judge or justice shall
-- src:8904 | (c) in any event, advise the prosecutor of their duty under subsection (3.2).
@ref s 486.4(3.1)(c) (src:8900-8904)
GIVEN `the prosecutor makes an application for an order under paragraph (2)(b) or (2.2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.4(3.1)(c) the presiding judge or justice must advise the prosecutor of their duty under subsection (3.2)` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor makes an application for an order under paragraph (2)(b) or (2.2)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the prosecutor makes an application for an order under paragraph (2)(b) or (2.2)(b)"

-- 486.4(3.2) If the prosecutor makes the application, they shall, as soon as feasible after the presiding judge or justice makes the order, inform the judge or justice that they have (a) informed the witnesses and the victim
-- who are the subject of the order of its existence; (b) determined whether they wish to be the subject of the order; and (c) informed them of their right to apply to revoke or vary the order.
-- src:8905 | Duty to inform
-- src:8906 | (3.2) If the prosecutor makes the application, they shall, as soon as feasible after the presiding judge or justice makes the order, inform the judge or justice that they have
-- src:8907 | (a) informed the witnesses and the victim who are the subject of the order of its existence;
-- src:8908 | (b) determined whether they wish to be the subject of the order; and
-- src:8909 | (c) informed them of their right to apply to revoke or vary the order.
@ref s 486.4(3.2) (src:8905-8909)
GIVEN `the prosecutor makes the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the presiding judge or justice makes the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.4(3.2) the prosecutor must inform the judge or justice of what they have done` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor makes the application` AND `the presiding judge or justice makes the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the prosecutor makes the application, they shall, as soon as feasible after the presiding judge or justice makes the order"

-- src:8905 | Duty to inform
-- src:8906 | (3.2) If the prosecutor makes the application, they shall, as soon as feasible after the presiding judge or justice makes the order, inform the judge or justice that they have
-- src:8907 | (a) informed the witnesses and the victim who are the subject of the order of its existence;
-- src:8908 | (b) determined whether they wish to be the subject of the order; and
-- src:8909 | (c) informed them of their right to apply to revoke or vary the order.
@ref s 486.4(3.2)(a), (b), (c) (src:8905-8909)
GIVEN `the prosecutor has informed the witnesses and the victim who are the subject of the order of its existence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor has determined whether they wish to be the subject of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor has informed them of their right to apply to revoke or vary the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.4(3.2) what the prosecutor informs the judge or justice of is complete` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor has informed the witnesses and the victim who are the subject of the order of its existence` AND `the prosecutor has determined whether they wish to be the subject of the order` AND `the prosecutor has informed them of their right to apply to revoke or vary the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "inform the judge or justice that they have (a) informed the witnesses and the victim who are the subject of the order of its existence; (b) determined whether they wish to be the subject of the order; and (c) informed them of their right to apply to revoke or vary the order"

-- 486.4(4) An order made under this section does not apply in either of the following circumstances: (a) the disclosure of information is made in the course of the administration of justice when the purpose of the disclosure is not one
-- of making the information known in the community; or (b) the disclosure of information is made by a person who is the subject of the order and is about that person and their particulars, in any forum and for any purpose, and they did
-- not intentionally or recklessly reveal the identity of or reveal particulars likely to identify any other person whose identity is protected by an order prohibiting the publication ...
-- src:8910 | Limitation
-- src:8911 | (4) An order made under this section does not apply in either of the following circumstances:
-- src:8912 | (a) the disclosure of information is made in the course of the administration of justice when the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known in the community; or
-- src:8913 | (b) the disclosure of information is made by a person who is the subject of the order and is about that person and their particulars, in any forum and for any purpose, and they did not intentionally or recklessly reveal the identity of or reveal particulars likely to identify any other person whose identity is protected by an order prohibiting the publication in any document or the broadcasting or transmission in any way of information that could identify that other person.
@ref s 486.4(4)(a), (b) (src:8910-8913)
GIVEN `the disclosure of information is made in the course of the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known in the community` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made by a person who is the subject of the order and is about that person and their particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they did not intentionally or recklessly reveal the identity of or reveal particulars likely to identify any other person whose identity is protected by an order prohibiting publication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.4(4) the order applies to the disclosure of information` MEANS
    IF    (`the disclosure of information is made in the course of the administration of justice` AND `the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known in the community`)
       OR (`the disclosure is made by a person who is the subject of the order and is about that person and their particulars` AND `they did not intentionally or recklessly reveal the identity of or reveal particulars likely to identify any other person whose identity is protected by an order prohibiting publication`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An order made under this section does not apply in either of the following circumstances"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply in either of the following circumstances"

-- 486.4(5) An order made under this section does not apply in respect of the disclosure of information by the victim or witness when it is not the purpose of the disclosure to make the information known to the public, including when the
-- disclosure is made to a legal professional, a health care professional or a person in a relationship of trust with the victim or witness.
-- src:8914 | Limitation — victim or witness
-- src:8915 | (5) An order made under this section does not apply in respect of the disclosure of information by the victim or witness when it is not the purpose of the disclosure to make the information known to the public, including when the disclosure is made to a legal professional, a health care professional or a person in a relationship of trust with the victim or witness.
@ref s 486.4(5) (src:8914-8915)
GIVEN `the disclosure is made by the victim or witness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the purpose of the disclosure to make the information known to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made to a legal professional, a health care professional or a person in a relationship of trust with the victim or witness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.4(5) the order applies to the disclosure of information by the victim or witness` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure is made by the victim or witness` AND (`the disclosure is made to a legal professional, a health care professional or a person in a relationship of trust with the victim or witness` OR (NOT `it is the purpose of the disclosure to make the information known to the public`))
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An order made under this section does not apply in respect of the disclosure of information by the victim or witness when it is not the purpose of the disclosure to make the information known to the public"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "when it is not the purpose of the disclosure to make the information known to the public"

§ `Section 486.5 -- Order restricting publication -- victims and witnesses`

-- 486.5(1) Unless an order is made under section 486.4, on application of the prosecutor in respect of a victim or a witness, or on application of a victim or a witness, a judge or justice may make an order directing that any information
-- that could identify the victim or witness shall not be published ... if the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order is in the interest of the proper administration of justice.
-- src:8917 | 486.5 (1) Unless an order is made under section 486.4, on application of the prosecutor in respect of a victim or a witness, or on application of a victim or a witness, a judge or justice may make an order directing that any information that could identify the victim or witness shall not be published in any document or broadcast or transmitted in any way if the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order is in the interest of the proper administration of justice.
@ref s 486.5(1) (src:8917)
GIVEN `an order is made under section 486.4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `who applies for the order` IS A `s 486.4 who applies`
      `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order is in the interest of the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.5(1) the judge or justice may make an order directing that information that could identify the victim or witness not be published` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an order is made under section 486.4` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless an order is made under section 486.4"
        IF ((`who applies for the order` EQUALS `s 486.4 the accused`) OR (`who applies for the order` EQUALS `s 486.4 a justice system participant`) OR (`who applies for the order` EQUALS `s 486.4 another person`)) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on application of the prosecutor in respect of a victim or a witness, or on application of a victim or a witness"
        IF `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order is in the interest of the proper administration of justice` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order is in the interest of the proper administration of justice"

-- 486.5(2.1) The offences for the purposes of subsection (2) are (a) an offence under section 423.1, 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13, or a serious offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization;
-- (b) a terrorism offence; (c) an offence under subsection 16(1) or (2), 17(1), 19(1), 20(1), 20.1(1), 20.2(1), 20.3(1), 20.4(1) or 22(1) of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act; or (d) an offence under subsection 21(1) or section 23
-- of that Act that is committed in relation to an offence referred to in paragraph (c).
-- src:8921 | (2.1) The offences for the purposes of subsection (2) are
-- src:8922 | (a) an offence under section 423.1, 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13, or a serious offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization;
@ref s 486.5(2.1)(a) (the sections) (src:8921-8922)
`s 486.5(2.1)(a) the listed offences` MEANS
    LIST
  (`s 487.04 listed provision` OF 423.1, "")
, (`s 487.04 listed provision` OF 467.11, "")
, (`s 487.04 listed provision` OF 467.111, "")
, (`s 487.04 listed provision` OF 467.12, "")
, (`s 487.04 listed provision` OF 467.13, "")

-- src:8924 | (c) an offence under subsection 16(1) or (2), 17(1), 19(1), 20(1), 20.1(1), 20.2(1), 20.3(1), 20.4(1) or 22(1) of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act; or
-- src:8925 | (d) an offence under subsection 21(1) or section 23 of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act that is committed in relation to an offence referred to in paragraph (c).
@ref s 486.5(2.1)(c), (d) (the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act provisions) (src:8924-8925)
`s 486.5(2.1)(c) the listed provisions of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act` MEANS
    LIST
  (`s 487.04 listed provision` OF 16, "(1)")
, (`s 487.04 listed provision` OF 16, "(2)")
, (`s 487.04 listed provision` OF 17, "(1)")
, (`s 487.04 listed provision` OF 19, "(1)")
, (`s 487.04 listed provision` OF 20, "(1)")
, (`s 487.04 listed provision` OF 20.1, "(1)")
, (`s 487.04 listed provision` OF 20.2, "(1)")
, (`s 487.04 listed provision` OF 20.3, "(1)")
, (`s 487.04 listed provision` OF 20.4, "(1)")
, (`s 487.04 listed provision` OF 22, "(1)")

DECLARE `s 486.5(2.1) where the offence is found` IS ONE OF
    `s 486.5(2.1) this Act`
    `s 486.5(2.1) the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act`
    `s 486.5(2.1) another instrument`

-- src:8921 | (2.1) The offences for the purposes of subsection (2) are
-- src:8922 | (a) an offence under section 423.1, 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13, or a serious offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization;
-- src:8923 | (b) a terrorism offence;
-- src:8924 | (c) an offence under subsection 16(1) or (2), 17(1), 19(1), 20(1), 20.1(1), 20.2(1), 20.3(1), 20.4(1) or 22(1) of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act; or
-- src:8925 | (d) an offence under subsection 21(1) or section 23 of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act that is committed in relation to an offence referred to in paragraph (c).
@ref s 486.5(2.1)(a) to (d) (src:8921-8925)
GIVEN `the provision of the Code or other instrument the offence is charged under` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `where the offence is found` IS A `s 486.5(2.1) where the offence is found`
      `s 2 serious offence: the offence is a serious offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 criminal organization: the offence was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 terrorism offence: the offence is a terrorism offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offence is committed in relation to an offence referred to in paragraph (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.5(2.1) the offence is one of the offences for the purposes of subsection (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`where the offence is found` EQUALS `s 486.5(2.1) this Act`) AND `s 487.04 the provision is on the list` `the provision of the Code or other instrument the offence is charged under` `s 486.5(2.1)(a) the listed offences` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`where the offence is found` EQUALS `s 486.5(2.1) this Act`) AND ((`s 2 serious offence: the offence is a serious offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`s 2 criminal organization: the offence was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`where the offence is found` EQUALS `s 486.5(2.1) this Act`) AND (`s 2 terrorism offence: the offence is a terrorism offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`where the offence is found` EQUALS `s 486.5(2.1) the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act`) AND `s 487.04 the provision is on the list` `the provision of the Code or other instrument the offence is charged under` `s 486.5(2.1)(c) the listed provisions of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`where the offence is found` EQUALS `s 486.5(2.1) the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act`) AND ((`the provision of the Code or other instrument the offence is charged under`'s `section` EQUALS 23) OR (`the provision of the Code or other instrument the offence is charged under`'s `section` EQUALS 21 AND `the provision of the Code or other instrument the offence is charged under`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")) AND `the offence is committed in relation to an offence referred to in paragraph (c)` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`where the offence is found` EQUALS `s 486.5(2.1) this Act`) AND ((`s 2 serious offence: the offence is a serious offence` EQUALS NOTHING) OR ((`s 2 serious offence: the offence is a serious offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`s 2 criminal organization: the offence was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization` EQUALS NOTHING)) OR (`s 2 terrorism offence: the offence is a terrorism offence` EQUALS NOTHING)) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is a serious offence, a criminal-organization offence or a terrorism offence is for the definitions of section 2 and section 467.1
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The offences for the purposes of subsection (2) are"

-- 486.5(2) On application of the prosecutor in respect of a justice system participant who is involved in proceedings in respect of an offence referred to in subsection (2.1), or on application of such a justice system participant,
-- a judge or justice may make an order directing that any information that could identify the justice system participant shall not be published ... if the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order is in the interest of the proper administration of justice.
-- src:8919 | (2) On application of the prosecutor in respect of a justice system participant who is involved in proceedings in respect of an offence referred to in subsection (2.1), or on application of such a justice system participant, a judge or justice may make an order directing that any information that could identify the justice system participant shall not be published in any document or broadcast or transmitted in any way if the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order is in the interest of the proper administration of justice.
@ref s 486.5(2) (src:8919)
GIVEN `s 2 justice system participant: the person is a justice system participant` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is involved in proceedings in respect of an offence referred to in subsection (2.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `who applies for the order` IS A `s 486.4 who applies`
      `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order is in the interest of the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.5(2) the judge or justice may make an order directing that information that could identify the justice system participant not be published` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT ((`s 2 justice system participant: the person is a justice system participant` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the person is involved in proceedings in respect of an offence referred to in subsection (2.1)`)) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of a justice system participant who is involved in proceedings in respect of an offence referred to in subsection (2.1)"
        IF (NOT ((`who applies for the order` EQUALS `s 486.4 the prosecutor`) OR (`who applies for the order` EQUALS `s 486.4 a justice system participant`))) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On application of the prosecutor in respect of a justice system participant who is involved in proceedings in respect of an offence referred to in subsection (2.1), or on application of such a justice system participant"
        IF `the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order is in the interest of the proper administration of justice` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the judge or justice is of the opinion that the order is in the interest of the proper administration of justice"

-- 486.5(3) An order made under this section does not apply in either of the following circumstances (the same words as 486.4(4)).
-- src:8927 | (3) An order made under this section does not apply in either of the following circumstances:
-- src:8928 | (a) the disclosure of information is made in the course of the administration of justice when the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known in the community; or
-- src:8929 | (b) the disclosure of information is made by a person who is the subject of the order and is about that person and their particulars, in any forum and for any purpose, and they did not intentionally or recklessly reveal the identity of or reveal particulars likely to identify any other person whose identity is protected by an order prohibiting the publication in any document or the broadcasting or transmission in any way of information that could identify that other person.
@ref s 486.5(3)(a), (b) (src:8927-8929)
GIVEN `the disclosure of information is made in the course of the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known in the community` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made by a person who is the subject of the order and is about that person and their particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they did not intentionally or recklessly reveal the identity of or reveal particulars likely to identify any other person whose identity is protected by an order prohibiting publication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.5(3) the order applies to the disclosure of information` MEANS
    IF    (`the disclosure of information is made in the course of the administration of justice` AND `the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known in the community`)
       OR (`the disclosure is made by a person who is the subject of the order and is about that person and their particulars` AND `they did not intentionally or recklessly reveal the identity of or reveal particulars likely to identify any other person whose identity is protected by an order prohibiting publication`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An order made under this section does not apply in either of the following circumstances"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply in either of the following circumstances"

-- 486.5(3.1) An order made under this section does not apply in respect of the disclosure of information by the victim, witness or justice system participant when it is not the purpose of the disclosure to make the information known
-- to the public, including when the disclosure is made to a legal professional, a health care professional or a person in a relationship of trust with the victim, or witness or justice system participant.
-- src:8930 | Limitation — victim, etc.
-- src:8931 | (3.1) An order made under this section does not apply in respect of the disclosure of information by the victim, witness or justice system participant when it is not the purpose of the disclosure to make the information known to the public, including when the disclosure is made to a legal professional, a health care professional or a person in a relationship of trust with the victim, or witness or justice system participant.
@ref s 486.5(3.1) (src:8930-8931)
GIVEN `the disclosure is made by the victim, witness or justice system participant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the purpose of the disclosure to make the information known to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made to a legal professional, a health care professional or a person in a relationship of trust with the victim, or witness or justice system participant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.5(3.1) the order applies to the disclosure of information by the victim, witness or justice system participant` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure is made by the victim, witness or justice system participant` AND (`the disclosure is made to a legal professional, a health care professional or a person in a relationship of trust with the victim, or witness or justice system participant` OR (NOT `it is the purpose of the disclosure to make the information known to the public`))
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An order made under this section does not apply in respect of the disclosure of information by the victim, witness or justice system participant when it is not the purpose of the disclosure to make the information known to the public"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "when it is not the purpose of the disclosure to make the information known to the public"

-- 486.5(4) An applicant for an order shall (a) apply in writing to the presiding judge or justice or, if the judge or justice has not been determined, to a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction in the judicial district where the
-- proceedings will take place; and (b) provide notice of the application to the prosecutor, the accused and any other person affected by the order that the judge or justice specifies.
DECLARE `s 486.5(4) to whom the application is made` IS ONE OF
    `s 486.5(4) the presiding judge or justice`
    `s 486.5(4) a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place`
    `s 486.5(4) another judge or justice`

-- src:8932 | Application and notice
-- src:8933 | (4) An applicant for an order shall
-- src:8934 | (a) apply in writing to the presiding judge or justice or, if the judge or justice has not been determined, to a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place; and
@ref s 486.5(4)(a) (src:8932-8934)
GIVEN `the application is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to whom the application is made` IS A `s 486.5(4) to whom the application is made`
      `the presiding judge or justice has been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.5(4)(a) the applicant has applied as required` MEANS
    IF `the application is in writing` AND (   (`the presiding judge or justice has been determined` AND (`to whom the application is made` EQUALS `s 486.5(4) the presiding judge or justice`))
                                             OR ((NOT `the presiding judge or justice has been determined`) AND (`to whom the application is made` EQUALS `s 486.5(4) a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place`)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An applicant for an order shall (a) apply in writing to the presiding judge or justice or, if the judge or justice has not been determined, to a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place"

-- src:8932 | Application and notice
-- src:8933 | (4) An applicant for an order shall
-- src:8935 | (b) provide notice of the application to the prosecutor, the accused and any other person affected by the order that the judge or justice specifies.
@ref s 486.5(4)(b) (src:8932-8935)
GIVEN `notice is given to the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice is given to the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice is given to any other person affected by the order that the judge or justice specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.5(4)(b) the applicant has provided notice of the application` MEANS
    IF `notice is given to the prosecutor` AND `notice is given to the accused` AND `notice is given to any other person affected by the order that the judge or justice specifies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provide notice of the application to the prosecutor, the accused and any other person affected by the order that the judge or justice specifies"

-- 486.5(5) An applicant for an order shall set out the grounds on which the applicant relies to establish that the order is necessary for the proper administration of justice.
-- src:8936 | Grounds
-- src:8937 | (5) An applicant for an order shall set out the grounds on which the applicant relies to establish that the order is necessary for the proper administration of justice.
@ref s 486.5(5) (src:8936-8937)
GIVEN `the applicant sets out the grounds on which the applicant relies to establish that the order is necessary for the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.5(5) the applicant has set out the grounds` MEANS
    IF `the applicant sets out the grounds on which the applicant relies to establish that the order is necessary for the proper administration of justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An applicant for an order shall set out the grounds on which the applicant relies"

-- 486.5(5.1) If the prosecutor makes an application for an order under subsection (1) or (2), the judge or justice shall (a) if the victim, witness or justice system participant is present, inquire of them if they wish to be the subject of
-- the order; (b) if not present, inquire of the prosecutor if, before the application was made, they determined whether ...; and (c) in any event, advise the prosecutor of their duty under subsection (8.2).
-- src:8938 | Duties — judge or justice
-- src:8939 | (5.1) If the prosecutor makes an application for an order under subsection (1) or (2), the judge or justice shall
-- src:8940 | (a) if the victim, witness or justice system participant is present, inquire of them if they wish to be the subject of the order;
-- src:8941 | (b) if the victim, witness or justice system participant is not present, inquire of the prosecutor if, before the application was made, they determined whether the victim, witness or justice system participant wishes to be the subject of the order; and
-- src:8942 | (c) in any event, advise the prosecutor of their duty under subsection (8.2).
@ref s 486.5(5.1)(a), (b), (c) (src:8938-8942)
GIVEN `the prosecutor makes an application for an order under subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the victim, witness or justice system participant is present` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 486.4(3.1) whom the presiding judge or justice must inquire of`
`s 486.5(5.1)(a), (b) the judge or justice must inquire` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the prosecutor makes an application for an order under subsection (1) or (2)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the prosecutor makes an application for an order under subsection (1) or (2)"
    ELSE IF `the victim, witness or justice system participant is present`
         THEN JUST `s 486.4(3.1) the victim or witness, whether they wish to be the subject of the order`
         ELSE JUST `s 486.4(3.1) the prosecutor, whether before the application was made they determined if the victim or witness wishes to be the subject of the order`

-- src:8938 | Duties — judge or justice
-- src:8939 | (5.1) If the prosecutor makes an application for an order under subsection (1) or (2), the judge or justice shall
-- src:8942 | (c) in any event, advise the prosecutor of their duty under subsection (8.2).
@ref s 486.5(5.1)(c) (src:8938-8942)
GIVEN `the prosecutor makes an application for an order under subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.5(5.1)(c) the judge or justice must advise the prosecutor of their duty under subsection (8.2)` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor makes an application for an order under subsection (1) or (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the prosecutor makes an application for an order under subsection (1) or (2)"

-- 486.5(6) The judge or justice may hold a hearing to determine whether an order should be made, and the hearing may be in private.
-- src:8943 | Hearing may be held
-- src:8944 | (6) The judge or justice may hold a hearing to determine whether an order should be made, and the hearing may be in private.
@ref s 486.5(6) (src:8943-8944)
GIVEN `the hearing is to determine whether an order should be made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.5(6) the judge or justice may hold a hearing, and the hearing may be in private` MEANS
    IF `the hearing is to determine whether an order should be made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may hold a hearing to determine whether an order should be made"

-- src:8946 | (7) In determining whether to make an order, the judge or justice shall consider
-- src:8947 | (a) the right to a fair and public hearing;
-- src:8948 | (b) whether there is a real and substantial risk that the victim, witness or justice system participant would suffer harm if their identity were disclosed;
-- src:8949 | (c) whether the victim, witness or justice system participant needs the order for their security or to protect them from intimidation or retaliation;
-- src:8950 | (d) society’s interest in encouraging the reporting of offences and the participation of victims, witnesses and justice system participants in the criminal justice process;
-- src:8951 | (e) whether effective alternatives are available to protect the identity of the victim, witness or justice system participant;
-- src:8952 | (f) the salutary and deleterious effects of the proposed order;
-- src:8953 | (g) the impact of the proposed order on the freedom of expression of those affected by it; and
-- src:8954 | (h) any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant.
@ref s 486.5(7) (the lead-in and factors) (src:8946-8954)
DECLARE `s 486.5(7) factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 486.5(7)(a) the right to a fair and public hearing`
    `s 486.5(7)(b) whether there is a real and substantial risk that the victim, witness or justice system participant would suffer harm if their identity were disclosed`
    `s 486.5(7)(c) whether the victim, witness or justice system participant needs the order for their security or to protect them from intimidation or retaliation`
    `s 486.5(7)(d) society’s interest in encouraging the reporting of offences and the participation of victims, witnesses and justice system participants in the criminal justice process`
    `s 486.5(7)(e) whether effective alternatives are available to protect the identity of the victim, witness or justice system participant`
    `s 486.5(7)(f) the salutary and deleterious effects of the proposed order`
    `s 486.5(7)(g) the impact of the proposed order on the freedom of expression of those affected by it`
    `s 486.5(7)(h) any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant`

@ref s 486.5(7) (src:8946-8954)
GIVEN f IS A `s 486.5(7) factor`
      `the judge or justice is determining whether to make an order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or justice considers the factor relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.5(7) the judge or justice must consider the factor` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the judge or justice is determining whether to make an order`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In determining whether to make an order"
    ELSE CONSIDER f
         WHEN `s 486.5(7)(h) any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant` THEN
             IF `the judge or justice considers the factor relevant`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE


-- 486.5(8) An order may be subject to any conditions that the judge or justice thinks fit.
-- src:8955 | Conditions
-- src:8956 | (8) An order may be subject to any conditions that the judge or justice thinks fit.
@ref s 486.5(8) (src:8955-8956)
GIVEN `the condition is one that the judge or justice thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.5(8) the order may be subject to the condition` MEANS
    IF `the condition is one that the judge or justice thinks fit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any conditions that the judge or justice thinks fit"

-- 486.5(8.1) If an order is made, the judge or justice shall, as soon as feasible, inform the victims, witnesses and justice system participants who are the subject of that order of its existence and of their right to apply to revoke or vary it.
-- src:8957 | Supplementary duty — judge or justice
-- src:8958 | (8.1) If an order is made, the judge or justice shall, as soon as feasible, inform the victims, witnesses and justice system participants who are the subject of that order of its existence and of their right to apply to revoke or vary it.
@ref s 486.5(8.1) (src:8957-8958)
GIVEN `an order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.5(8.1) the judge or justice must inform the victims, witnesses and justice system participants of the order's existence and of their right to apply to revoke or vary it` MEANS
    IF `an order is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an order is made, the judge or justice shall, as soon as feasible, inform the victims, witnesses and justice system participants"

-- 486.5(8.2) If the prosecutor makes the application, they shall, as soon as feasible after the judge or justice makes the order, inform the judge or justice that they have (a) informed ...; (b) determined ...; and (c) informed them of their right to apply to revoke or vary the order.
-- src:8959 | Duty to inform
-- src:8960 | (8.2) If the prosecutor makes the application, they shall, as soon as feasible after the judge or justice makes the order, inform the judge or justice that they have
-- src:8961 | (a) informed the victims, witnesses and justice system participants who are the subject of the order of its existence;
-- src:8962 | (b) determined whether they wish to be the subject of the order; and
-- src:8963 | (c) informed them of their right to apply to revoke or vary the order.
@ref s 486.5(8.2) (src:8959-8963)
GIVEN `the prosecutor makes the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or justice makes the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.5(8.2) the prosecutor must inform the judge or justice of what they have done` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor makes the application` AND `the judge or justice makes the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the prosecutor makes the application, they shall, as soon as feasible after the judge or justice makes the order"

-- src:8959 | Duty to inform
-- src:8960 | (8.2) If the prosecutor makes the application, they shall, as soon as feasible after the judge or justice makes the order, inform the judge or justice that they have
-- src:8961 | (a) informed the victims, witnesses and justice system participants who are the subject of the order of its existence;
-- src:8962 | (b) determined whether they wish to be the subject of the order; and
-- src:8963 | (c) informed them of their right to apply to revoke or vary the order.
@ref s 486.5(8.2)(a), (b), (c) (src:8959-8963)
GIVEN `the prosecutor has informed the victims, witnesses and justice system participants who are the subject of the order of its existence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor has determined whether they wish to be the subject of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor has informed them of their right to apply to revoke or vary the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.5(8.2) what the prosecutor informs the judge or justice of is complete` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor has informed the victims, witnesses and justice system participants who are the subject of the order of its existence` AND `the prosecutor has determined whether they wish to be the subject of the order` AND `the prosecutor has informed them of their right to apply to revoke or vary the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "inform the judge or justice that they have (a) informed the victims, witnesses and justice system participants who are the subject of the order of its existence; (b) determined whether they wish to be the subject of the order; and (c) informed them of their right to apply to revoke or vary the order"

-- 486.5(9) Unless the judge or justice refuses to make an order, no person shall publish in any document or broadcast or transmit in any way (a) the contents of an application; (b) any evidence taken, information given or submissions made
-- at a hearing under subsection (6); or (c) any other information that could identify the person to whom the application relates as a victim, witness or justice system participant in the proceedings.
-- The answer is the prohibition on any person, the accused included: JUST TRUE unless the judge or justice refused to make an order.
DECLARE `s 486.5(9) what would be published` IS ONE OF
    `s 486.5(9) the contents of an application`   -- (a)
    `s 486.5(9) any evidence taken, information given or submissions made at a hearing under subsection (6)`   -- (b)
    `s 486.5(9) any other information that could identify the person to whom the application relates as a victim, witness or justice system participant in the proceedings`   -- (c)
    `s 486.5(9) something else`

-- src:8964 | Publication prohibited
-- src:8965 | (9) Unless the judge or justice refuses to make an order, no person shall publish in any document or broadcast or transmit in any way
-- src:8966 | (a) the contents of an application;
-- src:8967 | (b) any evidence taken, information given or submissions made at a hearing under subsection (6); or
-- src:8968 | (c) any other information that could identify the person to whom the application relates as a victim, witness or justice system participant in the proceedings.
@ref s 486.5(9)(a), (b), (c) (src:8964-8968)
GIVEN `the judge or justice refuses to make an order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what would be published` IS A `s 486.5(9) what would be published`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.5(9) the person is prohibited from publishing, broadcasting or transmitting what would be published` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`what would be published` EQUALS `s 486.5(9) something else`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) the contents of an application; (b) any evidence taken, information given or submissions made at a hearing under subsection (6); or (c) any other information that could identify the person to whom the application relates"
        IF `the judge or justice refuses to make an order` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the judge or justice refuses to make an order, no person shall publish in any document or broadcast or transmit in any way"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 486.51 -- Application to vary or revoke an order`

-- 486.51(1) If a person who is the subject of an order made under section 486.4 or 486.5 requests that the prosecutor have it varied or revoked, the prosecutor shall, as soon as feasible, make an application to vary or revoke the order on their behalf.
-- src:8969 | Application — vary or revoke
-- src:8970 | 486.51 (1) If a person who is the subject of an order made under section 486.4 or 486.5 requests that the prosecutor have it varied or revoked, the prosecutor shall, as soon as feasible, make an application to vary or revoke the order on their behalf.
@ref s 486.51(1) (src:8969-8970)
GIVEN `the person is the subject of an order made under section 486.4 or 486.5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person requests that the prosecutor have the order varied or revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.51(1) the prosecutor must make an application to vary or revoke the order on the person's behalf` MEANS
    IF `the person is the subject of an order made under section 486.4 or 486.5` AND `the person requests that the prosecutor have the order varied or revoked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person who is the subject of an order made under section 486.4 or 486.5 requests that the prosecutor have it varied or revoked"

-- 486.51(2) If an application to vary or revoke an order made under section 486.4 or 486.5 is made by the person who is the subject of the order or by any other person, including a prosecutor, who is acting on their behalf, the court that made
-- the order or, if that court is for any reason unable to act, another court of equivalent jurisdiction in the same province shall, without holding a hearing, vary or revoke the order, unless the court is of the opinion that to do so may affect
-- the privacy interests of any person who is the subject of any order prohibiting the publication ... of information that could identify that person.
-- src:8971 | Order — vary or revoke
-- src:8972 | (2) If an application to vary or revoke an order made under section 486.4 or 486.5 is made by the person who is the subject of the order or by any other person, including a prosecutor, who is acting on their behalf, the court that made the order or, if that court is for any reason unable to act, another court of equivalent jurisdiction in the same province shall, without holding a hearing, vary or revoke the order, unless the court is of the opinion that to do so may affect the privacy interests of any person who is the subject of any order prohibiting the publication in any document or the broadcasting or transmission in any way of information that could identify that person.
@ref s 486.51(2) (src:8971-8972)
GIVEN `the application to vary or revoke is made by the person who is the subject of the order or by another person acting on their behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is of the opinion that varying or revoking the order may affect the privacy interests of any person who is the subject of any order prohibiting the publication of information that could identify that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.51(2) the court must vary or revoke the order without holding a hearing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the application to vary or revoke is made by the person who is the subject of the order or by another person acting on their behalf`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is made by the person who is the subject of the order or by any other person, including a prosecutor, who is acting on their behalf"
        IF `the court is of the opinion that varying or revoking the order may affect the privacy interests of any person who is the subject of any order prohibiting the publication of information that could identify that person` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the court is of the opinion that to do so may affect the privacy interests of any person who is the subject of any order prohibiting the publication"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 486.51(3) If the court is of the opinion that varying or revoking the order ... may affect the privacy interests of any person who is the subject of any order prohibiting the publication ..., the court shall hold a hearing.
-- src:8973 | Hearing
-- src:8974 | (3) If the court is of the opinion that varying or revoking the order that is the subject of an application referred to in subsection (2) may affect the privacy interests of any person who is the subject of any order prohibiting the publication in any document or the broadcasting or transmission in any way of information that could identify that person, the court shall hold a hearing to determine whether the order should be varied or revoked.
@ref s 486.51(3) (src:8973-8974)
GIVEN `the court is of the opinion that varying or revoking the order may affect the privacy interests of any person who is the subject of any order prohibiting the publication of information that could identify that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.51(3) the court must hold a hearing to determine whether the order should be varied or revoked` MEANS
    IF `the court is of the opinion that varying or revoking the order may affect the privacy interests of any person who is the subject of any order prohibiting the publication of information that could identify that person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court is of the opinion that varying or revoking the order that is the subject of an application referred to in subsection (2) may affect the privacy interests of any person"

-- 486.51(4) In order to determine whether the order should be varied, the court shall take into account whether it is possible to do so in a manner that protects the privacy interests of any other person who is the subject of any order
-- prohibiting the publication ... of information that could identify that person.
-- src:8975 | Factor
-- src:8976 | (4) In order to determine whether the order should be varied, the court shall take into account whether it is possible to do so in a manner that protects the privacy interests of any other person who is the subject of any order prohibiting the publication in any document or the broadcasting or transmission in any way of information that could identify that person.
@ref s 486.51(4) (src:8975-8976)
GIVEN `the court is determining whether the order should be varied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.51(4) the court must take into account whether it is possible to vary the order in a manner that protects the privacy interests of any other person` MEANS
    IF `the court is determining whether the order should be varied`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In order to determine whether the order should be varied"

-- 486.51(5) The applicant is not required to provide notice of the application to vary or revoke the order to the accused.
-- src:8977 | Notice
-- src:8978 | (5) The applicant is not required to provide notice of the application to vary or revoke the order to the accused.
@ref s 486.51(5) (src:8977-8978)
GIVEN `the application is an application to vary or revoke an order made under section 486.4 or 486.5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.51(5) the applicant is required to provide notice of the application to vary or revoke the order to the accused` MEANS
    IF `the application is an application to vary or revoke an order made under section 486.4 or 486.5`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The applicant is not required to provide notice of the application to vary or revoke the order to the accused"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of an application to vary or revoke

-- 486.51(6) The accused shall not be permitted to make submissions in relation to the application.
-- src:8979 | Submissions
-- src:8980 | (6) The accused shall not be permitted to make submissions in relation to the application.
@ref s 486.51(6) (src:8979-8980)
GIVEN `the submissions are in relation to the application to vary or revoke the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.51(6) the accused is permitted to make submissions in relation to the application` MEANS
    IF `the submissions are in relation to the application to vary or revoke the order`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The accused shall not be permitted to make submissions in relation to the application"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of submissions in relation to the application

-- 486.51(7) If the order is varied or revoked, the prosecutor shall notify the accused.
-- src:8981 | Notice of change
-- src:8982 | (7) If the order is varied or revoked, the prosecutor shall notify the accused.
@ref s 486.51(7) (src:8981-8982)
GIVEN `the order is varied or revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.51(7) the prosecutor must notify the accused` MEANS
    IF `the order is varied or revoked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the order is varied or revoked, the prosecutor shall notify the accused"

§ `Section 486.6 -- Offence`

-- 486.6(1) Every person who fails to comply with an order made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
-- The orders "under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3)" are those made under subsections (1), (2), (2.1), (2.2) and (3) of section 486.4.
-- src:8983 | Offence
-- src:8984 | 486.6 (1) Every person who fails to comply with an order made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 486.6(1) (src:8983-8984)
GIVEN `the order` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 486.6(1) the order is one made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2)` MEANS
        (`the order`'s `section` EQUALS 486.4 AND (   `the order`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR `the order`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)" OR `the order`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2.1)"
                                                    OR `the order`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2.2)" OR `the order`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(3)"))
     OR (`the order`'s `section` EQUALS 486.5 AND (`the order`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR `the order`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)"))

-- src:8983 | Offence
-- src:8984 | 486.6 (1) Every person who fails to comply with an order made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 486.6(1) (src:8983-8984)
GIVEN `the order is one made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to comply with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.6(1) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` MEANS
    IF `the order is one made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2)` AND `the person fails to comply with the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who fails to comply with an order made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2)"

-- The punishment the section states: it names the class (summary conviction) and no fine or imprisonment; the general summary-conviction penalty is fixed in another part (section 787), not among these sources.
-- src:8983 | Offence
-- src:8984 | 486.6 (1) Every person who fails to comply with an order made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 486.6(1) (the punishment) (src:8983-8984)
`s 486.6(1) the punishment the section states` MEANS Punishment WITH
    `mode`                   IS `on summary conviction`
    `maximum imprisonment`   IS `no imprisonment is stated`
    `minimum imprisonment`   IS `no imprisonment is stated`
    `maximum fine`           IS `no fine is stated`
    `minimum fine`           IS `no fine is stated`

-- 486.6(1.1) A prosecutor shall not commence or continue a prosecution against a person who is the subject of the order unless, in the opinion of the prosecutor, (a) the person knowingly failed to comply with the order;
-- (b) the privacy interests of another person who is the subject of any order prohibiting the publication ... have been compromised; and (c) a warning to the individual is not appropriate.
-- The answer is the bar on the prosecutor: JUST TRUE where the person is the subject of the order and the three opinions are not all held.
-- src:8985 | Prosecution — limitation
-- src:8986 | (1.1) A prosecutor shall not commence or continue a prosecution against a person who is the subject of the order unless, in the opinion of the prosecutor,
-- src:8987 | (a) the person knowingly failed to comply with the order;
-- src:8988 | (b) the privacy interests of another person who is the subject of any order prohibiting the publication in any document or the broadcasting or transmission in any way of information that could identify that person have been compromised; and
-- src:8989 | (c) a warning to the individual is not appropriate.
@ref s 486.6(1.1)(a), (b), (c) (src:8985-8989)
GIVEN `the person is the subject of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the prosecutor the person knowingly failed to comply with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the prosecutor the privacy interests of another person who is the subject of any order prohibiting the publication of information that could identify that person have been compromised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the prosecutor a warning to the individual is not appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.6(1.1) the prosecutor is barred from commencing or continuing a prosecution against the person who is the subject of the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person is the subject of the order`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "against a person who is the subject of the order"
        IF `in the opinion of the prosecutor the person knowingly failed to comply with the order` AND `in the opinion of the prosecutor the privacy interests of another person who is the subject of any order prohibiting the publication of information that could identify that person have been compromised` AND `in the opinion of the prosecutor a warning to the individual is not appropriate` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless, in the opinion of the prosecutor,"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 486.6(2) For greater certainty, an order referred to in subsection (1) applies to prohibit, in relation to proceedings taken against any person who fails to comply with the order, the publication ... of information that could identify a victim,
-- witness or justice system participant whose identity is protected by the order.
-- src:8990 | Application of order
-- src:8991 | (2) For greater certainty, an order referred to in subsection (1) applies to prohibit, in relation to proceedings taken against any person who fails to comply with the order, the publication in any document or the broadcasting or transmission in any way of information that could identify a victim, witness or justice system participant whose identity is protected by the order.
@ref s 486.6(2) (src:8990-8991)
GIVEN `the proceedings are taken against a person who fails to comply with an order referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 486.6(2) the order applies to prohibit the publication of information that could identify a victim, witness or justice system participant in those proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are taken against a person who fails to comply with an order referred to in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to proceedings taken against any person who fails to comply with the order"
